{"seq":14,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-mcp-instructions-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:07:12.541Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"6d5c7574fc863ceaf24ee395db759e68a4b887c6f13071df0575ae3445fddf93","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Hollis. I checked all six of Moss's notes in the public share. Two of them have ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n1. *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated). Thea Ramaswell logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The same note says it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n2. *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Thea submitted it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers on the 04:00 shift at Doors 14–18 in Eau Claire weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it the same evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the next morning's shift got through fine. The note also says to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n\nA few things to check before this goes in the deck:\n• Marcus's note \"Q2 expansion wrap\" (14 Jul 2025) also mentions #4419 for QFL, but he describes it as Gate 3 printer lag, not a scanner problem. The two descriptions don't match, so please confirm with support or Dana before using it.\n• Moss's other QFL notes (9/14 pipeline digest, 3/23 renewal check-in) mention the account but give no ticket numbers.\n• The tickets #4409 and #4412 in Moss's Central handoffs note are for Marrow, not QFL. Watch out for \"Quarendon Freightways\" too: that's a different company and not a customer.\n\nThese are notes written by Moss, not the support system itself, so the ticket queue may have more QFL tickets than these."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":15,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-mcp-instructions-opus-gbrain-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T08:07:18.479Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"cf4ddff9820b8eaa9f496c98e9bf81c32a39f887731ea5aee34b7d8512391232","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I sent Hollis the list in his DM. Moss has six notes in the public share, and two of them give ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n1. **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\", which has no date. Thea Ramaswell logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n2. **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Thea opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Doors 14–18 in Eau Claire weren't getting text messages with their bay assignments. Support fixed it that evening, and Thea confirmed the next morning that it worked.\n\nI also told him to check a few things before using these in the deck:\n- **#4419 doesn't match across notes.** Marcus's 14 Jul 2025 note gives the same number for Quarrendon but calls it Gate 3 printer lag, not a scanner problem. I suggested he confirm with support or Dana Okafor, who now runs the account.\n- **Two of Moss's other notes mention the account without ticket numbers:** the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in.\n- **Some tickets and names belong to other accounts.** #4409 and #4412 in Moss's Central handoffs note are for Marrow, not Quarrendon. \"Quarendon Freightways\" is a different company and isn't a customer.\n- **This may not be every ticket.** These come from Moss's notes, not the support system, so the support queue may hold more Quarrendon tickets.\n\nEverything came from public notes, and ticket numbers are operational facts rather than money figures, so no approval was needed."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
